  "Id": "5a0b0485-7a55-4bf4-ae23-04f51d890334"/*FractalNoise*/,
  "Description": "Generates fractal noise (also known as pink or fractional noise) by layering several octaves of noise.\n\nIt can be used to create patterns that look like clouds, smoke, dust or scratches on film.\n\nAKA: perlin, simplex, fbm, clouds, turbulence\n\nSee also: [TileableNoise], [WorleyNoise], [ShardNoise], [Grain]",
